1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,600
Each string carries 60 detectors,

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:06,500
spaced 17 meters apart,

3
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:11,500
extending from a depth of 1.5 kilometers to 2.5 kilometers.

4
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:15,200
There are 86 of these strings,

5
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:19,200
with standard strings spaced about 125 meters apart,

6
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:23,800
forming an observatory that spans roughly one cubic kilometer of ice.

7
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:28,200
This lets us follow particles step by step.

8
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:32,000
But detecting them is not quite that simple.
